{["DictKey_descriptionNeutralsTask_4"] = "", ["DictKey_sortie_5"] = "MiG-29A FULCRUM - Operational Conversion Course - Caucasus", ["DictKey_descriptionText_1"] = "MiG-29A FULCRUM - OPERATIONAL CONVERSION COURSE\nCAUCASUS / KOBULETI - DCS TRAINING CAMPAIGN\n\nMISSION\nAn English-language conversion of Iron87Ita's nine-exercise dynamic campaign for DCS: MiG-29A Fulcrum Full Fidelity (9.12A). Four Client positions start HOT at the original Kobuleti locations. The original coalitions represent the trainee force and simulated opposition in a fictional training setting.\n\nAIRCRAFT AND LOADOUT\nInitial loadout: 2 R-27R, 2 R-73, centreline fuel tank and GSh-30-1. Internal fuel: 3376 kg. Countermeasures: 30 chaff and 30 flare. Rearm on the ground with module-compatible FAB/OFAB bombs or S-8 rockets for air-to-ground exercises. Retain air-to-air capability for combined exercises. No air-to-air refuelling is available.\n\nEXECUTION\nPrepare the aircraft and verify radio tuning and SN-29/DTC navigation data before taxi. Check the recovery airfield selection. Dynamic target positions are not uploaded automatically to the navigator. Use the live F10 map and ground-observer coordinates, then acquire ground targets visually.\nR-862 presets: CH0/CH1 Kobuleti 133.000 AM; CH2 Batumi 131.000; CH3 Kutaisi 134.000; CH4 Senaki 132.000; CH5 flight 124.000. Verify the actual cockpit/DTC setting before calling ATC.\nRearm before departure. Once ready airborne, select F10 > MiG-29A TRAINING CAMPAIGN > CAMPAIGN MISSIONS. Air contacts spawn immediately relative to the requesting group's current position and direction. START NEXT IN SEQUENCE selects the first incomplete exercise in the requesting player's record; every exercise can also be selected and repeated individually.\n\nTRAINING PROGRAMME\n01 VISUAL FIGHTER ENGAGEMENT\n02 AIR DEFENCE INTERCEPT\n03 BVR INTERCEPT\n04 HIGH-ALTITUDE INTERCEPT\n05 LOGISTICS CONVOY STRIKE\n06 ARMOURED INTERDICTION\n07 SHORT-RANGE AIR DEFENCE ATTACK\n08 COMBINED ARMS EXERCISE\n09 FINAL OPERATIONAL EVALUATION\nPhase 1 develops visual acquisition, N019, IRST, HMS, R-27R/R-73 and cannon employment. Phase 2 retains conventional ground attack as a secondary capability. Phase 3 integrates both tasks. Air opposition scales one-for-one with active BLUE pilots, maximum four; ground strength remains fixed. A solo pilot faces a MiG-25PD in Exercise 04 and a MiG-21bis in Exercise 09, following the original ordering.\n\nTRAINING RULES\nFOX 1 / FOX 2 only. Reference trainee weapons: R-27R and R-73. No FOX 3 or R-27ER/ET in the programme. Identify contacts positively before firing. In Exercise 01 both sides wait until the first neutral merge; AI carry R-60M only. The trainee may rearm with R-73 only for a comparable visual exercise. The campaign does not lock the rearming menu to these choices: observe the rules as a training requirement.\nGround attack uses unguided weapons and visual target acquisition. No targeting pod, laser-guided ordnance or anti-radiation missile is provided. The retained JTAC is a range observer: its 1688 laser is an external reference, not a laser spot the Fulcrum can track or a source of weapon guidance. The aircraft's own laser rangefinder is a different system. SPO-15LM silence does not rule out an IR threat. Manage fuel and any required ground rearming; the campaign imposes no arbitrary numerical BINGO or attack profile.\n\nRANGES AND ASSESSMENT\nAll ground scenarios use the original eight SPAWN ZONE GROUND areas. One area is selected randomly; units are placed inside it in clear terrain. A failed layout aborts the spawn. ACTIVE MISSION BRIEF repeats tasking and remaining objectives.\nOriginal scoring: +25 per air kill, +10 per ground kill and +100 for the first completion of each exercise. Automatic completion requires all correctly spawned objectives to be destroyed. An incomplete spawn suspends credit: restart that exercise. Participating/active BLUE pilots receive campaign credit. Recovery, identification and airmanship are not graded automatically. Recover at Kobuleti after each sortie.\n\nRECORDS\nF10 > MY TRAINING RECORD. Dedicated MiG progress file: Saved Games/DCS/Missions/Saves/MiG29ATrainingFF/progress.dat. Cross-session persistence works only when io/lfs are already available. The normal sandbox gives SESSION ONLY progress. No host DCS configuration files are changed. F10 menus remain shared at flight-group level, as in the original; record queries and START NEXT use the first active player in that group, while kill and completion records are stored by player name.\n\nVERSION 1.1 FF EN\nEnglish cover and eight-page English kneeboard included. The range diagram is a schematic of DCS local coordinates, not a terrain/navigation chart. See the official module manual for cockpit procedures and aircraft limitations. Structural and simulated-script checks do not replace Mission Editor and in-flight validation.\nOriginal campaign: Iron87Ita. Personal Full Fidelity conversion; not an official Eagle Dynamics campaign.\n", ["DictKey_descriptionBlueTask_3"] = "MiG-29A Fulcrum Full Fidelity / four Client positions HOT at Kobuleti. Nine progressive exercises via F10 > MiG-29A TRAINING CAMPAIGN. Rearm before departure and select an exercise when ready airborne. R-27R/R-73; conventional FAB/OFAB/S-8 ground attack. Kobuleti CH0/CH1 133.000 AM. Ground observer coordinates; no tanker. English cover and kneeboard included.", ["DictKey_descriptionRedTask_2"] = ""}
